  "html": "<article data-article-id=\"ab6f2bb9-4dbc-4030-84e5-2068dc9c5518\">\n  <figure><img src=\"/images/articles/ab6f2bb9-4dbc-4030-84e5-2068dc9c5518-1.jpg\" alt=\"Sunlight streaming through trees in mist\"></figure>\n  <p class=\"poem\">Flee, dark night!<br>Joyful sunlight, drive all evil away!<br>World, I want no more of your honor, pride, and power.<br>I want to love you, Lord, alone!<br>Let the sun of your favor shine on my heart, since Christ<br>the Beloved has carried my sins away.</p>\n  <p>-Wolfgang Sailer, ca. 1500-1550<br>-Songbook of the Hutterian Brethren, #283</p>\n</article>\n",
